<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  GUL-437 / GUL-617: daily factory-guard self-test on the Air. Zero model, zero tokens.

  GUL-617 moved this from ~/Library/LaunchAgents (gui/501) to a SYSTEM LaunchDaemon.
  Why: this Mac is a headless appliance, not a desktop. On 2026-10-29 at 09:39:16
  WindowServer was killed by the userspace watchdog (OS_REASON_WATCHDOG; spin report
  WindowServer_2026-10-29-093900_paperclip.userspace_watchdog_timeout.spin). The Aqua
  session was torn down and the machine sat at the login window from then on. A gui/501
  LaunchAgent cannot fire while nobody is logged in, so the canary went quiet in silence —
  exactly the failure it exists to catch. A system LaunchDaemon with UserName=paperclip
  needs no login session and survives a WindowServer death.

  Fires at 04:45 Warsaw wall time, before the 05:30 PM round. The Mac's system
  timezone is Europe/Berlin, which carries the same UTC offset and the same EU
  DST rules as Europe/Warsaw all year, so system-local 04:45 IS 04:45 Warsaw —
  no TZ trick needed (launchd only understands system-local wall time anyway).

  Install (person, after the PR merge) — entry and plist both come from
  origin/main, never from a shared-checkout working tree (concurrent agent
  runs park it on other branches; a repo-path entry then fails at 04:45 in
  silence, proven by GUL-437's first kickstart after merge #65):
    mkdir -p ~/paperclip-agents/factory-selftest
    git -C ~/Projects/homelab-2nd show origin/main:agents/factory/selftest/guard-selftest.sh > ~/paperclip-agents/factory-selftest/guard-selftest.sh
    chmod +x ~/paperclip-agents/factory-selftest/guard-selftest.sh
    git -C ~/Projects/homelab-2nd show origin/main:agents/factory/selftest/dev.voitech.factory-guard-selftest.plist > /tmp/guard-selftest.plist
    sudo install -m 0644 -o root -g wheel /tmp/guard-selftest.plist /Library/LaunchDaemons/dev.voitech.factory-guard-selftest.plist
    sudo launchctl bootout system/dev.voitech.factory-guard-selftest 2>/dev/null || true
    sudo launchctl bootstrap system /Library/LaunchDaemons/dev.voitech.factory-guard-selftest.plist
    # pre-GUL-617 gui agent: remove it, or the job is scheduled twice a day
    rm -f ~/Library/LaunchAgents/dev.voitech.factory-guard-selftest.plist
  Run once now:
    sudo launchctl kickstart -k system/dev.voitech.factory-guard-selftest
  Result:
    tail ~/paperclip-agents/majster/factory/selftest.log
    sudo launchctl print system/dev.voitech.factory-guard-selftest | head -20
  The self-test drift-checks its own installed entry and plist against
  origin/main every run, so a skipped install is caught the next morning.

  UserName is required: a LaunchDaemon defaults to root, and the guard, the repo
  checkout and the state dir all belong to paperclip. HOME is set explicitly
  because launchd does not guarantee it for system daemons, and every default in
  the script is $HOME-based.

  PATH must carry /opt/homebrew: launchd's default has no pi, node or brew git.
  The script re-execs the origin/main copy of itself, so a stale installed
  entry still tests what main says. Missed window (machine asleep) = no run,
  nothing stops; launchd fires the missed calendar event on the next wake. A
  FAIL writes .../factory/STOP and the factory refuses to start until a person
  clears it. launchd stdout/stderr go next to selftest.log for the case where
  the script itself never starts.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>dev.voitech.factory-guard-selftest</string>
  <key>UserName</key>
  <string>paperclip</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>/Users/paperclip/paperclip-agents/factory-selftest/guard-selftest.sh</string>
  </array>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    <key>HOME</key>
    <string>/Users/paperclip</string>
  </dict>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Hour</key>
    <integer>4</integer>
    <key>Minute</key>
    <integer>45</integer>
  </dict>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/paperclip/paperclip-agents/majster/factory/launchd.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/paperclip/paperclip-agents/majster/factory/launchd.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
